  "details": "I'm pretty sure VRChat doesn't try to clear the Heap memory during loading(the perfect time for it) nor when avatars changes. The proof for it is that, over time, even after hopping worlds, memory still inscreases more and more, reaching over 10GB like it did for me the other day(which made performance get hit severely). \n\nSo, since memory leak is and has been a problem for ages now, why not just call System.GC.Collect(); or make use of some other similar method while downloading a new world and once again every time 5-10 people change avatars within a world?",
